# SF114: the offline lines reader (lines by situation: subtitle plus mumble)
#
# Intent: with no host and no model the unit answers a situation from a canned line on a pantry shelf: the line is shown as the subtitle (when the subtitle setting allows) and played as the
#   code-made mumble. The pantry core accepts record kind 5 (line, 100 bytes at most, the extra is the situation tag). The reader (maipai_lines.cc) loads the household language's shelf, picks a line
#   that is not the last one used for that situation (30 s cooldown per situation), frees the shelf at once, and does nothing when no shelf or no line exists, so the recorded clips stay as they are
#   then. Hooked: link lost and back (the recorded back clip plays only when no line was said), wake heard with no host, head pet, face tap, lifted, set down, shake, timer done, low battery
#   (the recorded warning stays). Not hooked yet: loud noise, good night, the three greetings (no event point in the device code). A bench tool self.lines.say drives it.
# Placement: unit (body half); the host seeds the shelves.
# Upstream: none (MaiPai code only).
# Check after a flash: self.lines.say {situation: touch_head} with a seeded line shelf installed shows the subtitle and mumbles (silent at volume 0); with no shelf it answers ok false and nothing changes.
# Kconfig: none (under the pantry and asset store switches).
# Memory cost: nothing while idle; while picking, the shelf copy (up to 40 KB PSRAM) and 101 bytes of stack, freed straight after.

